    "name": "new/codespan_backslash_emphasis.md",
    "markdown": "Note that `\\` or `/` _will_ be interpreted as path separators on Windows, and will match against `/` in glob expressions.\n\nUse `C:\\Users\\` for **home** and `D:\\` for data.\n\n`a\\` *b* `c`\n\n\\`*escaped tick*\\` `code`\n\n`\\` ``\\`` **after double backticks**\n\n_``\\`_``\n\n_`` a`_ ``\n",
    "html": "<p>Note that <code>\\</code> or <code>/</code> _will_ be interpreted as path separators on Windows, and will match against <code>/</code> in glob expressions.</p>\n<p>Use <code>C:\\Users\\</code> for **home** and <code>D:\\</code> for data.</p>\n<p><code>a\\</code> *b* <code>c</code></p>\n<p>`<em>escaped tick</em>` <code>code</code></p>\n<p><code>\\</code> <code>\\</code> <strong>after double backticks</strong></p>\n<p><em>```</em>``</p>\n<p>_<code>a`_</code></p>\n",
    "sanitizedHtml": "<p>Note that <code>\\</code> or <code>/</code> _will_ be interpreted as path separators on Windows, and will match against <code>/</code> in glob expressions.</p>\n<p>Use <code>C:\\Users\\</code> for **home** and <code>D:\\</code> for data.</p>\n<p><code>a\\</code> *b* <code>c</code></p>\n<p>`<em>escaped tick</em>` <code>code</code></p>\n<p><code>\\</code> <code>\\</code> <strong>after double backticks</strong></p>\n<p><em>```</em>``</p>\n<p>_<code>a`_</code></p>\n"
